WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.850
The original Star Wars trilogy is constantly
evolving and that's not necessarily a good

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:05.850
thing.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:09.900
Now, with the arrival of Disney+, we've been
given yet another version of Star Wars: A

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.550
New Hope, the very first film in the franchise.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:16.820
And this version includes a head-scratching
change to A New Hope's most controversial

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.599
scene: The moment when "Han shoots first"
… or does he?

00:00:20.599 --> 00:00:23.490
Now, technically, this new change wasn't Disney's
doing.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.460
Like all the other perplexing Star Wars changes
that have been made since the "Special Editions"

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:32.910
were first released in 1997, this latest edit
is the work of creator George Lucas.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:37.360
He's still finding new, groundbreaking ways
to rile up Star Wars fans, all these years

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.950
after selling the franchise.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:42.000
This was confirmed in a statement that Disney
gave to ComicBook.com:

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.150
"The change was made by George Lucas, prior
to the Disney acquisition."

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:51.020
Meanwhile, in a Twitter exchange between Uproxx
Senior Entertainment Editor Mike Ryan and

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:54.670
longtime Lucasfilm employee Pablo Hidalgo,
Ryan tweeted:

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:57.770
"I just watched the new Greedo scene from
the first Star Wars.

00:00:57.770 --> 00:00:58.790
WHAT ON EARTH?!?!"

00:00:58.790 --> 00:00:59.790
Hidalgo responded:

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:03.200
"Ah, I see D+ must have the 4K version.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.560
[...] This would've been done a few years
back, by Lucas.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:10.920
A final 4K restoration in anticipation of
a 3D re-release that never happened after

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.460
3D re-releases fizzled."

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:17.260
In the latest version of the scene, bounty
hunter Greedo utters a perplexing word right

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:23.780
before his infamous shootout with Han Solo…
and it's really quite the doozy.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.030
"Maclunkey!"

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:26.280
Maclunkey?

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.819
Thanks for clearing that up!

00:01:27.819 --> 00:01:32.049
There are no subtitles when Greedo shouts
this strange word even though we're treated

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:35.630
to subtitles for the rest of Greedo's dialogue
throughout the scene.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:37.229
So what does it mean, exactly?

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:39.340
Well, Slate helpfully points out that

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:43.810
"'Ma klounkee' is a phrase used in The Phantom
Menace [...] which is translated in the subtitles

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:45.280
as […] 'It will be the end of you.'"

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.969
"Next time we race, boy, it will be the end
of you."

00:01:49.969 --> 00:01:54.799
If we have our dates correct, Lucas made this
change prior to selling Lucasfilm to Disney

00:01:54.799 --> 00:01:59.090
in 2012, but after the film's last Blu-ray
release in 2011.

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:00.529
That's a pretty small window.

00:02:00.529 --> 00:02:05.689
In the original cut of the scene the one that
played in theaters in 1977 there's absolutely

00:02:05.689 --> 00:02:07.929
no question that Han shoots first.

00:02:07.929 --> 00:02:11.870
That's why he's slyly pulling his blaster
from its holster while chatting up Greedo.

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:15.069
Not only does Han shoot first, Han only shoots!

00:02:15.069 --> 00:02:16.930
Greedo doesn’t even get off a shot.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:18.760
Try putting that on a t-shirt…

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:22.850
It's a cold-blooded move but actually rather
important for his character arc, since he

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.439
becomes a better man over the course of the
film.

00:02:25.439 --> 00:02:30.050
Well, for the film's 1997 Special Edition
re-release, Lucas altered the scene so that

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:34.909
Greedo fires a shot at Han and misses, prompting
Han to fire back in self defense.

00:02:34.909 --> 00:02:38.930
This change absolves Han of any questionable
behavior, but one could argue that it also

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:40.950
makes his character arc less compelling.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.750
Still, George Lucas doesn't see it that way
at all.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:45.959
As he told The Hollywood Reporter in 2012,

00:02:45.959 --> 00:02:50.940
"[The re-edit] upset people because they wanted
Solo to be a cold-blooded killer, but he actually

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:51.940
isn't."

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.689
Where do you stand on this brouhaha?

00:02:53.689 --> 00:02:58.519
"Sorry about the mess."

00:02:58.519 --> 00:03:02.371
Following the release of next month's Star
Wars Episode IX: The Rise of Skywalker, the

00:03:02.371 --> 00:03:05.480
immediate future of Star Wars hinges on Disney+.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.769
Luckily for fans, the streaming service has
big plans in store for the franchise, and

00:03:09.769 --> 00:03:14.959
you can stream the original trilogy, the prequel
trilogy, Rogue One: A Star Wars Story, and

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:17.180
Star Wars Episode VII: The Force Awakens.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:21.650
Meanwhile, The Last Jedi and Solo: A Star
Wars Story will hit the streamer when current

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:23.640
distribution agreements expire.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:28.060
Disney+ will also be streaming The Rise of
Skywalker once the film leaves theaters.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:33.240
Right now, you can also stream The Clone Wars
on Disney+ both the film and the series.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:39.040
Or go nuts and stream Star Wars Rebels, Star
Wars Resistance, loads of Lego Star Wars content,

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:43.640
shorts, and documentaries and, of course,
The Mandalorian , the new series created by

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.520
Jon Favreau that's raking in rave reviews.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:50.310
There's also a live-action series in the works
that will follow the adventures of Rogue One's

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:55.920
Cassian Andor, as well as the recently-announced
and long-anticipated live-action Obi-Wan Kenobi

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:56.920
series.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:01.470
That will star Ewan McGregor, reprising his
role as the Jedi Master after portraying him

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:02.819
in the prequel films.

00:04:02.819 --> 00:04:07.099
In other words, Disney+ is shaping up to be
the go-to destination for fans to get their

00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:09.280
Star Wars fix for the next few years.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.709
Until then… may the force be with you.

00:04:11.709 --> 00:04:14.569
Oh, and one more thing:

00:04:14.569 --> 00:04:16.579
"Maclunkey!"

